WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.600
when creating word documents there will

00:00:01.839 --> 00:00:06.240
be situations where you need to display

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.080
certain information in a table format

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.360
word has tools within itself to allow

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.480
you to do this

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.960
and i'm going to demonstrate them here

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.279
the first way to insert a table is to go

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.560
to the insert tab and click on that

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:22.880
and then select the table icon and

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.320
just below there as i start to move my

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.720
mouse down

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:29.439
the rows and then across it

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.439
automatically starts to insert

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:32.480
that amount of columns and rows within

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:33.680
to the letter

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.680
when i'm happy with the number of

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.760
columns and rules i want just click

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.360
and it will automatically insert them

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.840
the problem there is is that i still

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.719
need to

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.320
populate the table an alternative to

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:45.520
this is importing information from

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.520
another document

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:51.199
and then converting that into a table

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.879
the first thing i'm going to do is undo

00:00:51.199 --> 00:00:56.239
that

00:00:52.879 --> 00:00:57.600
so that is now clear i will then open

00:00:56.239 --> 00:00:59.440
the spreadsheet that i downloaded from

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.920
the vision alone website which contains

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.600
the information that i'm going to use

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.280
so what i need to do is i need to copy

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.400
this information so i'll click

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.720
and hold and drag it down and across and

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.479
then select the copy icon

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.320
now that i have copied that information

00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:17.200
i can then go back to the letter

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.880
and select paste so as you can see it

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.920
has now pasted the information

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.799
into the letter i now have several

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.720
options

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:26.560
so if i click on the little drop down on

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.840
the paste options button

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.680
it gives me the option to keep the

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.640
source formatting

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.479
use the destination styles link and keep

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:37.759
source formatting

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:40.240
link and use destination styles insert

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:41.759
as a picture or keep the text on me

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.920
for this example i'm going to keep the

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:45.600
text only

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.840
so as you can see it has now inserted

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.240
that text into the letter

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.520
but it isn't presented in a very nice

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.960
format

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.560
what i need to do now is i need to

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:57.360
convert that text

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.079
into a table to do that i need to

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.680
highlight

00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:02.560
all of the text and then go back to the

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.520
insert tab

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:08.800
so i click on insert and go to table and

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:10.879
then select convert text to table

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.560
so word is actually identifying where

00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:14.720
the spacing is occurring

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.400
within each of those pieces of text and

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.080
it's automatically identified that it

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.040
needs to have three columns and eight

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:22.319
rows

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:25.599
it is separated by the tabs

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:28.160
so i click ok that will insert the text

00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:29.680
into a table

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.680
once i have the information into the

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.360
table i then want to apply some

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.800
formatting

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.720
if i double click on the icon at the top

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.319
left of the table it will open up the

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:43.599
table design tab

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:46.239
from there i can apply table styles

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:47.599
shading border styles variety of

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:49.280
different things

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:51.360
in this example all i'm going to do is

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:55.280
just to add some shading

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:57.840
to the top border once that's done

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:02.080
and i'm happy that it looks okay i can

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.080
then save the document